{"agent_id":"pp3g-HJkE-r3-exploratory-pass-427-under-epic-423-inventory-what","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-23T20:21:25.697553599Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"a0c44591-c703-4710-a6c1-0af8287813e2","comment_uuid":"b5c5b435-4652-4016-8594-cdcdc380c6ad","author":"pp3g-HJkE-r3-exploratory-pass-427-under-epic-423-inventory-what","content":"# R3 — Fork Deltas vs Stock 1.x, Mapped to OpenCode 2 Parity (Issue #427, EPIC #423)\n\n> Breadth-first evidence gathering, NOT exhaustive source audit. Read-only pass under /tmp/opencode/r3.\n\n## 0. Method & Sources (in required order)\n\n| # | Source | Result |\n|---|--------|--------|\n| 1 | `.crosslink/knowledge/opencode-fork.md` | **ABSENT** at that path. Live `.crosslink/knowledge/` contains only `agent-orchestration-playbook.md`, `crosslink-fork.md`, `kickoff-custom-template.md`, `model-discipline.md`. Fork knowledge is instead materialised as `fork/opencode-src/` + patch history. WHAT-NOT-TESTED: whether the page was renamed/moved behind a different knowledge key; cache-dir rename was checked (`.crosslink/.knowledge-cache` also absent in worktree). |\n| 2 | `fork/opencode-src` git log/history | **Present.** Durable export at `792cdbe3` (`feat(fork): durable export…`) with applyable patch `958 lines`, commit graph pin `a105350` (upstream v1.18.13) → `a7a80ef` (fork branch `pp3g-fork-v1.18.13`). Live tree is that patched source. |\n| 3 | Wrapper `~/.local/bin/opencode` | **Verified.** Marker `Body read timed out` count `2` on `REAL` binary `/home/claude-code/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.3/lib/node_modules/opencode-ai/bin/opencode.exe`; fallback to `--version` contains `fork` (`1.18.13-pp3g-fork`). Cites lineage #154/#138/#142/#129 in guard comment; fail-closed on marker loss (#274). |\n| 4 | `.crosslink/knowledge/model-discipline.md` touches fork behaviour | **Verified.** Grok ban (§Forbidden: xAI/Grok NEVER; \"patched out of `opencode models`\") + `chunkTimeout` provider options + request-vs-task timeout distinction. Actual grok filter lives at user-level plugin `~/.config/opencode/plugins/plugin.ts` (blacklist + regex sweep), not in the core patch. |\n| 5 | `docs/research/agent-tooling-and-permission-enforcement.md` §2.1/§2.7/§4 | **Verified.** Describes fork as `1.18.13-pp3g-fork` silent-hang epic (#156), `safeIterable()` fix (commit `98dfe4a`), separate DB `opencode-fork-pp3g.db` via `InstallationChannel`, provider timeout user-level config. |\n| 6 | OpenCode 2 changelog/release notes/docs | **Fetched live:** `opencode.ai/changelog` through `v1.18.21` (2026-08-21), `opencode.ai/v2/docs` + `v2/docs/migrate-v1`, and `github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/dev/packages/core/src/v1/config/config.ts` raw (192 lines). No OpenCode 2 stable release; `opencode2` beta (`@opencode-ai/cli@beta`) is the \"will-become-2.0\" line. |\n\nLocal patch inspected at `/tmp/opencode/r3/patch.diff` (`git show 792cdbe3:fork/patches/opencode-fork-v1.18.13-pp3g.patch`).\n\n---\n\n## 1. Delta Inventory (pp3g fork vs stock 1.18.13) — 9 rows\n\n> Columns: delta | what it does | why added (issue refs) | v2 status | evidence | risk-if-fork-retired.\n> Each row carries WHY / WHAT / HOW-CERTAIN / WHAT-NOT-TESTED per AGENTS.md reasoning-certainty.\n\n### D1 — `wrapBodyIdle` / `bodyIdleTimeout` + `bodyAbsoluteTimeout` (non-SSE idle-progress deadline)\n\n| field | value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **What it does** | Adds a per-chunk idle timer for non-SSE `Response.body` (JSON / other) that resets on every chunk: `wrapBodyIdle(res, ms, ctl, absoluteMs)` aborts via `ProviderError.ResponseStreamError(\"Body read timed out\")` only when a body stalls ≥ `bodyIdleTimeout` between chunks; optional `bodyAbsoluteTimeout` is a total wall-clock cap (off by default). SSE bodies continue to use `wrapSSE(chunkTimeout)`. Schema adds `provider.<id>.options.bodyIdleTimeout` + `bodyAbsoluteTimeout` (+ `openapi.json`). Implemented in both `packages/core/src/aisdk.ts` (plain `Error`) and `packages/opencode/src/provider/provider.ts` (`ResponseStreamError`). Pattern preserves hy3 F2: slow-but-progressing bodies never abort. |\n| **Why added** | Companions to `chunkTimeout` for the non-SSE path uncovered while hardening the silent-hang family. Prevents a provider that stops emitting bytes mid-body from hanging forever below the SSE layer. |\n| **V2 status** | **STILL-ABSENT** (v1 tip) / **UNKNOWN-NEEDS-PROBE** (v2 beta provider schema). |\n| **Evidence** | `fork/patches/…patch: +wrapBodyIdle` in both files; `packages/core/src/v1/config/provider.ts:bodyIdleTimeout/bodyAbsoluteTimeout`; `packages/sdk/openapi.json: +bodyIdleTimeout/bodyAbsoluteTimeout`; live `fork/opencode-src/packages/opencode/src/provider/provider.ts:89,1826,1867`; stock dev `packages/core/src/v1/config/config.ts` (192-line raw fetched) has NO `bodyIdleTimeout`/`llmIdleTimeout`; `opencode.ai/changelog` v1.18.14–v1.18.21 mentions no such fields; `v2/docs/migrate-v1` lists provider migration (`provider`→`providers`, `npm`→`package`, `options`→`settings/headers/body`) but does not mention these new options (they are not in \"accepted but unsupported\" either — genuinely new, so absent unless re-added under v2's new `providers.<id>.settings` shape). |\n| **Risk if retired** | **MEDIUM.** Non-SSE stalls would revert to unbounded wait (or only the outer `timeout:60 min`). Lower exposure than SSE hangs but still a silent-hang leg. Mitigated partly by D2 turn-level guard (D2 fires above this layer), but body-level observability + bounded scope are lost. Agent-launch safety degrades on providers/tests that exercise non-SSE bodies (GZIP / HEALTHY_JSON / title path). |\n| **WHY** | Idle-progress deadline is the correct primitive for non-SSE: it aborts only stalled bodies, never penalising slow-but-progressing ones. Evidence: patch comment \"slow-but-progressing body is never aborted (hy3 F2 preserved)\", unit test `body-idle-timeout.test.ts` covers stall vs slow-pass. |\n| **WHAT** | Claim based on patch diff (958-line export), live patched source (`provider.ts:89`, `aisdk.ts:77`), schema (`provider.ts:118`), openapi diff, and absence in fetched upstream dev `config.ts`. |\n| **HOW CERTAIN** | **Evidence-based** (file:line-verified; upstream absence confirmed via live fetch of the dev-branch file and changelog word-search). |\n| **WHAT-NOT-TESTED** | Did NOT run the harness `body-idle-timeout.test.ts` or a live 16-row body-idle row against `opencode2` beta to probe v2 parity; did NOT decode v2's compiled `Provider` schema from a running `opencode2` binary. |\n\n### D2 — `llmIdleTimeout` + `Stream.timeoutOrElse` turn-level guard (+ instrumentation) in `session/llm.ts`\n\n| field | value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **What it does** | Mandatory per-parsed-event idle guard: `config.experimental.llmIdleTimeout` (default 300 s) wraps `Stream.fromAsyncIterable(safeIterable(fullStream))` via `Stream.timeoutOrElse(duration, orElse → ResponseStreamError(\"Turn stalled: no parsed stream event within …ms\"))`. Fires for *any* stall above the raw-body layer — the only mechanism that bounds the production 10.9 h signature (parsed-event stalls). Also emits `llm stream start` + per-event `llm stream event / elapsedSinceLastParsedEventMs` debug logs for self-identifying next hang (#191 instrumentation). |\n| **Why added** | Issue #191 MAJOR + epic #156. Raw-body timeouts (D1) cannot bound stalls that occur after chunks are parsed (SDK / stream adapter layer). This is the *deterministic* upper bound for the longest observed silent hang. Config lives in `packages/core/src/v1/config/config.ts:llmIdleTimeout`. |\n| **V2 status** | **STILL-ABSENT** (v1 tip) / **UNKNOWN-NEEDS-PROBE** (v2 beta experimental). |\n| **Evidence** | `fork/patches/…patch: llm.ts:+llmIdleTimeout/+Stream.timeoutOrElse`; `packages/core/src/v1/config/config.ts:+llmIdleTimeout`; live `fork/opencode-src/packages/opencode/src/session/llm.ts:411–436` (comments cite #191, `timeoutFail does NOT exist` note); upstream dev `config.ts` raw fetched (192 lines, `experimental` only has `disable_paste_summary/batch_tool/openTelemetry/primary_tools/continue_loop_on_deny/mcp_timeout/policies` — NO `llmIdleTimeout`); `opencode.ai/changelog` never mentions \"Turn stalled\" / \"llmIdleTimeout\"; `v2/docs/migrate-v1` lists `batch_tool/openTelemetry/primary_tools/continue_loop_on_deny` as *accepted but unsupported* (ignored with warning) — `llmIdleTimeout` is not listed because it never existed upstream to be ignored (i.e., absent). |\n| **Risk if retired** | **CRITICAL — agent-launch killer.** This is the sole bound on parsed-event stalls. Without it, a single provider stall above the body layer reproduces the indefinite hang; kickoff `timeout` only caps total agent runtime (playbook §5.3) and does not abort the hung provider call itself. Wrapper marker `Body read timed out` would also stop firing for this class. Historical precedent: laguna s-2.1-free #129 stall (outgoing `message=stream` with no response, zero ERROR). |\n| **WHY** | Turn-level idle semantics (\"checked for each pull\" per effect) is the required primitive; raw-body timers cannot see parsed-event time. Evidence: 10.9 h production stall class, verified `timeoutOrElse` per-pull idle behaviour in effect 4.0.0-beta.83. |\n| **WHAT** | Claim based on patch hunk, live `llm.ts:411–436`, schema absence in fetched upstream `config.ts`, changelog verbal search. |\n| **HOW CERTAIN** | **Evidence-based** (same verification as D1). |\n| **WHAT-NOT-TESTED** | Did NOT probe a running `opencode2` beta's resolved config schema (e.g. `opencode2 debug config`) for a renamed equivalent; did NOT replay the 10.9 h stall reproduction against upstream or v2 beta. |\n\n### D3 — `safeIterable()` consumption-deadlock fix (the durable silent-hang killer)\n\n| field | value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **What it does** | Wraps the AI SDK `fullStream` AsyncIterable so `Effect.Stream.fromAsyncIterable` scope finalizer never blocks on `iter.return()` after a provider stream error. `return()` is fired fire-and-forget (`void Promise.resolve(iter.return?.()).catch(()=>{})`) and a synthetic `{done:true}` is returned immediately, letting the failure propagate without deadlocking `runDrain` (the #154 signature). Lives in `packages/opencode/src/session/llm.ts:43–60`, comment cites `af98d ? safeIterable()` lineage. |\n| **Why added** | Reliability epic #156 / fork commit `98dfe4a` (preserved per docs). Root cause was NOT a stuck provider but a consumption deadlock in `llm.ts`: `effect Stream.fromAsyncIterable` awaited `iter.return()` that rejects/hangs after `wrapBodyIdle/wrapSSE` aborts, deadlocking the runner into a silent hang. User-level `chunkTimeout` alone could not fix it because the error was swallowed by the deadlock. Separate DB channel (`InstallationChannel` → `opencode-fork-pp3g.db`) isolates verification noise. |\n| **V2 status** | **STILL-ABSENT** (v1 tip) / **OBSOLETE-REDESIGNED / UNKNOWN-NEEDS-PROBE** (v2 beta). |\n| **Evidence** | `fork/patches/…patch: llm.ts:+safeIterable`; live `fork/opencode-src/packages/opencode/src/session/llm.ts:36–60`; `docs/research/agent-tooling-and-permission-enforcement.md:§2.1` attributes fix to `safeIterable()` fire-and-forget; upstream changelog v1.18.14 notes \"Preserved structured mid-stream provider errors so compatible providers can retry\" and v1.18.11 \"Stopped MCP SSE connections from getting stuck in reconnect loops\" — adjacent retry fixes but NOT this `Stream.fromAsyncIterable` deadlock pattern; no mention of `safeIterable` / `return()` hang. v2 beta is a redesigned session core (effect-based `SessionV2` / `SessionExecution` per specs); the defect may be obsolete if v2 no longer uses `Stream.fromAsyncIterable(fullStream)` in the same way — OR it may still be present under a new shape. Without code probe, treat as UNKNOWN. |\n| **Risk if retired** | **CRITICAL — highest.** This is the durable cure for the original killer hang; all timeouts (D1/D2/D4) depend on the stream being able to surface the abort error. Retiring before upstream fixes the same deadlock re-introduces the silent hang even with timeouts configured. Wrapper marker count would drop to 0, failing closed (#274 invariant) and blocking launches by design. |\n| **WHY** | A timeout without a non-deadlocking consumption path is insufficient; the SDK's `return()` contract after error is the deadlock site. Evidence: 2026-08-06 verification found `wrapBodyIdle` absolute timer firing but error never reaching SDK consumer — the #226 binary-vs-source divergence, resolved only by this return-path fix. |\n| **WHAT** | Claim based on patch, live `llm.ts:43–60`, docs §2.1 citation of `98dfe4a`, upstream changelog negative search, valid reasoning about v2 core redesign. |\n| **HOW CERTAIN** | **Evidence-based** for v1 tip (absent); **Guess** for v2 beta (redesigned vs still-present needs code probe — flagged as such). |\n| **WHAT-NOT-TESTED** | Did NOT diff `opencode2` beta `session/llm.ts` equivalent; did NOT replay the deadlock reproduction against upstream or beta. The cheapest discriminating test (run source vs binary with an injected stall) exists in `fork/harness` but was not executed in this read-only pass. |\n| **Marker signal** | `~/.local/bin/opencode` guard counts `\"Body read timed out\"` ≥2 via `grep -ac` on the binary + `Turn stalled` string. Live fork binary hits `2` (`provider.ts` + `aisdk.ts`); stock `a105350` hits `0`. |\n\n### D4 — Bounded retry budget `RETRY_MAX_RETRIES=2` + `RETRY_BOUNDED_CODES` (3 POSTs total)\n\n| field | value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **What it does** | Caps retries for the timeout/stream error class (`ProviderResponseStreamError`, `ProviderHeaderTimeoutError`, `ECONNRESET`, `ZlibError`) to exactly 3 POSTs (`initial + 2`, `RETRY_MAX_RETRIES=2`). Scheduler adds jitter and respects `Retry-After`. All other errors (429 / usage-limit / 5xx) keep existing unbounded retry-after semantics. Terminal `WARN totalPOSTs=meta.attempt` bookkeeping. File: `packages/opencode/src/session/retry.ts:30–54,213`. |\n| **Why added** | Without a bound, a deterministic failure (e.g. decompression error introduced by re-wrapping compressed bodies, or a repeatable stall) retries forever → retry storm. Issue #407 evidence + v1.18.17 changelog \"Capped automatic session retries and added jitter to reduce repeated retry storms\" is the upstream *adjacent* fix; upstream's cap is not known to match this per-code bounded set or the 3-POST invariant, and does not include `ZlibError` determinism guard explicitly. Fork fix also required #273 `retries:0` companion (see D5). |\n| **V2 status** | **ALREADY-IN-V2 (partially) / STILL-ABSENT (exact semantics).** Upstream v1.18.17 now caps retries generically with jitter (per changelog). The fork's per-code bound (exact 3 POSTs, `ZlibError` included, exhaustive enumeration) has NO verbal parity in changelog. Treat as *partially* landed upstream, but the specific invariant is still fork-only. v2 beta status: **UNKNOWN-NEEDS-PROBE** (retry policy likely redesigned around `SessionExecution`). |\n| **Evidence** | `fork/patches/…patch: +RETRY_MAX_RETRIES/+RETRY_BOUNDED_CODES`; live `fork/opencode-src/packages/opencode/src/session/retry.ts:30,213`; `opencode.ai/changelog v1.18.17`: \"Capped automatic session retries and added jitter\"; `opencode.ai/changelog v1.18.20`: \"Retry more network error variants … Retry xAI capacity…\" — broader retry expansion but no `ProviderResponseStreamError`/3-POST language. Upstream dev `retry.ts` not fetched in this pass (negative inference via changelog). |\n| **Risk if retired** | **MEDIUM.** Without the bound, a deterministic `ProviderResponseStreamError`/`ZlibError` loops indefinitely (or until outer agent timeout, burning quota/time). Cost/burn risk, not immediate silence, but still degrades agent reliability under the exact error class the fork turns into retriable signals. |\n| **WHY** | Bounded retries for deterministic failures prevent infinite cost; `ZlibError` must not retry forever because body re-wrapping can introduce it deterministically. Evidence: retry matrix in `fork/tests/retry.test.ts` (5 bounded-budget tests). |\n| **WHAT** | Claim based on patch, live `retry.ts:30`, changelog verbal match for generic cap, gap analysis for per-code set. |\n| **HOW CERTAIN** | **Evidence-based** for fork shape; **Proven** that upstream now has *some* cap (v1.18.17 entry), but **Evidence-based (weak)** that semantics are NOT identical (changelog wording mismatch). |\n| **WHAT-NOT-TESTED** | Did NOT fetch upstream `retry.ts` source to compare `RETRY_BOUNDED_CODES` membership vs upstream cap logic; did NOT run the 5 bounded-budget tests against `opencode2` beta. |\n\n### D5 — Title-generation `retries:0` pin (`session/prompt.ts`) — fixes 4-POST-vs-3 root cause\n\n| field | value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **What it does** | Pins `maxRetries: input.retries ?? 0` (i.e. `0`) for the `small_model` title-generation stream (`SessionPrompt` title request uses `retries:0`), so a mid-stream `Body read timed out` / idle error on this secondary request does NOT trigger AI-SDK retries on top of the fork's 3-POST budget. Without it, the 16-row matrix row 1 showed 4 POSTs instead of 3. File: `packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts:235–238` (+ row at `1316`). Issue #273 hardening, #235 root-cause. |\n| **Why added** | Companionship invariant: D4's 3-POST budget governs the main turn; an extra retry in the small `small_model` title path double-counts and breaks the harness's `meta.attempt` accounting. |\n| **V2 status** | **STILL-ABSENT** (v1 tip) / **UNKNOWN-NEEDS-PROBE** (v2 beta title agent). |\n| **Evidence** | Patch hunk not in 958-line base export (it landed after `9e898aa1` / `c7d6e241`); live file `fork/opencode-src/packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts:235–238` comment cites `#273` / `#235 row-1 4-POST-vs-3`; stock v1 `prompt.ts` not fetched but changelog has no title-retry entry. v2 `migrate-v1` maps `small_model` → `agents.title.model` but says nothing about title retry pin. |\n| **Risk if retired** | **LOW** (scope-limited). Main-turn hang safety unchanged, but matrix invariant breaks and title generation can spuriously add a 4th POST under stall, confusing retry accounting and costing an extra provider call. |\n| **WHY** | Secondary request must not share the main retry budget; pinning to 0 keeps the `ProviderResponseStreamError` path deterministic. Evidence: harness `run-matrix.sh` row 1 delta from 4→3 after fix. |\n| **WHAT** | Claim based on live `prompt.ts:235` comment + commit notes `9e898aa1`, not on patch diff alone. |\n| **HOW CERTAIN** | **Evidence-based** for live fork; **Guess** for upstream absence (negative search only). |\n| **WHAT-NOT-TESTED** | Did NOT fetch stock `prompt.ts` to confirm missing pin (inferred from changelog + patch absence); did NOT check `opencode2` `agents.title` retry shape. |\n\n### D6 — `sdk/openapi.json` schema exposure (provider `bodyIdle/bodyAbsolute` + `llmIdleTimeout`)\n\n| field | value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **What it does** | Exposes the new provider `bodyIdleTimeout`/`bodyAbsoluteTimeout` option schemas and `experimental.llmIdleTimeout` to OpenAPI / SDK generation. Without it, the fields exist at runtime but are invisible to `sdk` clients and `debug config` tooling. |\n| **Why added** | API surface completeness; generated `types.gen.ts` / `types.gen.d.ts` blocks. |\n| **V2 status** | **STILL-ABSENT** (by construction — v2 beta has new `providers` / `experimental` contracts). v2 lists `logLevel/server/subagent_depth/compaction.tail_turns/prune/batch_tool/openTelemetry/primary_tools/continue_loop_on_deny/provider id/whitelist/blacklist/...` as accepted-but-unsupported / ignored. `bodyIdleTimeout` etc. are not listed because they never existed to be ignored — i.e. absent in v2 surface as well, pending explicit re-add. |\n| **Evidence** | `fork/patches/…patch: +sdk/openapi.json hunk`; live `fork/opencode-src/packages/sdk/openapi.json` contains the new fields; `v2/docs/migrate-v1#accepted-but-unsupported-fields` enumerates ignored legacy fields and does not mention them (negative evidence of absence). |\n| **Risk if retired** | **NEGLIGIBLE** (discoverability only). Runtime guard still works without OpenAPI; SDK clients just cannot discover/configure the fields via generated types. |\n| **WHY** | Schema exposure completes the configuration contract for timeout fields. |\n| **WHAT** | Patch-hunk-verified + v2 migrate doc cross-check. |\n| **HOW CERTAIN** | **Evidence-based**. |\n| **WHAT-NOT-TESTED** | Did NOT check v2 beta's generated OpenAPI/SDK for a renamed equivalent. |\n\n### D7 — Version suffix `pp3g-fork` + `InstallationChannel` / DB split (`opencode-fork-pp3g.db`)\n\n| field | value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **What it does** | Compile-time `OPENCODE_VERSION='1.18.13-pp3g-fork'` + `OPENCODE_CHANNEL='fork-pp3g'` (via `Script.version`/`Script.channel` → `define: { OPENCODE_VERSION, OPENCODE_CHANNEL }` in `packages/opencode/script/build.ts` & `packages/cli/script/build.ts`), surfaced at runtime as `opencode --version → 1.18.13-pp3g-fork`. `InstallationChannel` then selects `~/.local/share/opencode/opencode-fork-pp3g.db` vs `opencode.db` (`packages/core/src/database/database.ts:54`). Enables wrapper fail-closed identity check, hub-cache disambiguation, and verification isolation. |\n| **Why added** | Support/identity (hardening #274 — survive `autoupdate:false` loss), diagnose \"sessions gone\" (#313), prevent fork verification noise polluting prod history. |\n| **V2 status** | **OBSOLETE-REDESIGNED** (v2 beta). Upstream `InstallationChannel` logic persists (`database.ts:49` channel-tagged DB name), but the `pp3g-fork` channel/value is fork-only. v2 beta installs as separate binary `opencode2` with its own install directory (`opencode.ai/v2/docs` intro: \"installs and runs as `opencode2`, does not replace `opencode`\"), so fork channel is moot. The *capability* (channel-tagged DB) is already upstream; the *value* `fork-pp3g` is not. |\n| **Evidence** | `fork/opencode-src/packages/core/src/installation/version.ts:6` + `packages/core/src/database/database.ts:54` (`opencode-${InstallationChannel}…db`); build scripts `packages/script/src/index.ts: env.OPENCODE_VERSION / CHANNEL`; live `opencode --version → 1.18.13-pp3g-fork`; `~/.local/bin/opencode` guard + `docs/research/agent-tooling-and-permission-enforcement.md:§2.1` channel note; `opencode.ai/v2/docs` beta notes `opencode2` binary name, not channel. |\n| **Risk if retired** | **LOW for safety, MEDIUM for operability.** Hang cure does not depend on version string; but without it, the \"which binary am I running\" observability + wrapper drift guard disappear, and fork DB history merges with production DB. v2's `opencode`/`opencode2` split already gives binary disambiguation outside the channel mechanism. |\n| **WHY** | Identity + fail-closed wrapper + DB isolation are operator concerns, not stream correctness; they prevent silent fork loss (#274) but are separable from the abort path itself. |\n| **WHAT** | Build-script + runtime file-verified, v2 intro doc cross-check. |\n| **HOW CERTAIN** | **Evidence-based** (file:line + live `opencode --version` + wrapper `grep -c`). |\n| **WHAT-NOT-TESTED** | Did NOT verify v2 beta's `opencode2 --version` channel string or its DB path. |\n\n### D8 — Test fixtures `body-idle-timeout.test.ts` + `retry.test.ts` extensions\n\n| field | value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **What it does** | Adds 7 provider tests (`stall abort`, `slow-but-progressing pass`, `absolute cap`, `SSE vs non-SSE dispatcher`, `absent content-type` — `packages/opencode/test/provider/body-idle-timeout.test.ts`) and 5 bounded-budget tests (`retry.test.ts` + `RETRY_MAX_RETRIES` assertions). Preservation in `fork/patches` makes them portable. Not runtime code but gates the hang fixes in CI/harness. |\n| **Why added** | Keep the hang fixes from regressing; matrix harness `fork/harness/run-matrix.sh` + `server.js` drives the 16-row functional gate (90 s outer kill per hang row). |\n| **V2 status** | **OBSOLETE-REDESIGNED** (test path moved / new harness). Tests live under `packages/opencode/test/…`; v2 beta test layout is redesigned (`packages/core` vs `packages/opencode` split + effect migration). Behavioural intent would need re-porting to v2's runner. |\n| **Evidence** | `fork/patches/…patch: +test/provider/body-idle-timeout.test.ts` + `test/session/retry.test.ts` hunks; live files `fork/opencode-src/packages/opencode/test/provider/body-idle-timeout.test.ts:57,154,182` etc.; upstream changelog has no mention of these tests. |\n| **Risk if retired** | **LOW** (verification debt). Runtime behaviour unchanged if D1–D5 stay, but regression guard gone until upstream adds equivalent harness rows. |\n| **WHY** | Tests are the regression pin for the timeout class; without them the durable fix can silently regress (as it did pre-#226). |\n| **WHAT** | Patch-hunk-verified; upstream absence via changelog negative search. |\n| **HOW CERTAIN** | **Proven** for fork addition; **Guess** for v2 harness shape (not probed). |\n| **WHAT-NOT-TESTED** | Did NOT run the tests; did NOT locate equivalent v2 beta test directory. |\n\n### D9 — `models.dev` / Grok catalog \"patch\" + provider `chunkTimeout` hygiene (seed deltas)\n\n| field | value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **What it does** | Two separable ideas the seed conflates: (a) *Grok/xAI blacklist*: forbid `grok*` / `x-ai` family via regex across every provider's model list (`FORBIDDEN_MODEL_PATTERNS` → `/(^|[-\\/.])grok(-|\\.|$)/i`) + explicit `opencode-go` blacklist (`grok-4.5`, `grok-code`, …) plus cache-merge filter. (b) *Provider timeout hygiene*: `provider.opencode/go.options: timeout 60 min + headerTimeout/chunkTimeout 5 min` in `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json` (user-level global, not in-repo). Both are **NOT** in `fork/patches/…patch` (958-line diff has zero `models.dev` / `grok` / `FORBIDDEN` occurrence). They live in the user-level plugin `~/.config/opencode/plugins/plugin.ts` (+ `dynamic-models.ts`) and user-level `opencode.json`. |\n| **Why added** | (a) Policy #347 / #249: xAI/Grok permanently forbidden (operator standing rule). (b) #103 whitelist + #156 reliability: `chunkTimeout: 300s` cures the hung-stream leg at request scope; user-level placement ensures it reaches every kickoff agent (project-level `.opencode/opencode.json` would not). |\n| **V2 status** | **STILL-ABSENT (fork core) / OBSOLETE-REDESIGNED (v2 config shape) / IN-SITU (user-level plugin persists independently of fork).** The fork binary never carried this patch; retiring the fork binary does NOT remove the user-level plugin — the plugin continues to hide grok from `opencode models` on both `opencode` and `opencode2` as long as the file stays. v2 provider schema (`provider`→`providers`, `options`→`settings/headers/body`, see `v2/docs/migrate-v1#providers`) re-spells timeout fields entirely; the v1 `chunkTimeout` name is legacy. Upstream docs `opencode.ai/docs/config#models` still documents `provider.<id>.options.chunkTimeout` so the legacy name is not gone in v1, but v2 native shape is `providers.<id>.settings.baseURL/headers/body`. |\n| **Evidence** | Negative patch grep: `grep -c \"grok\\|FORBIDDEN\\|models.dev\" /tmp/opencode/r3/patch.diff → 0`; `~/.config/opencode/plugins/plugin.ts: FORBIDDEN_MODEL_PATTERNS + opencode-go blacklist + whitelist(7 Zen models: big-pickle/…/north-mini-code-free) + cache-merge filter`; `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json: provider.opencode/go.options.{timeout:3600000,headerTimeout:300000,chunkTimeout:300000}` (30 s in docs example, 300 s in deployment); `opencode.ai/docs/config#models` still lists `chunkTimeout`; `v2/docs/migrate-v1` says v1 `chunkTimeout` → v2 `mcp.timeout.*` split for MCP but provider `chunkTimeout` mapping under providers is via `settings/headers/body` separation (not a 1-1 name). |\n| **Risk if retired** | **LOW for fork retirement; MEDIUM-HIGH if user-level plugin also removed.** Fork retirement alone keeps grok hidden (plugin is not fork code). If the plugin is also deleted, `opencode models opencode-go` would immediately re-list `grok-4.5` (ships in built-in catalog) and violate standing rule #249; model-discipline violation would be silent until launch. Timeout hygiene: `chunkTimeout` would survive in `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json` (also not fork code) — but if that file is reset to defaults without re-adding the 5-min value, SSE hangs revert. |\n| **WHY** | Catalog filtering is operator policy enforcement; timeout hygiene is the request-scoped companion to stream timeouts. Neither is a compile-time fork change. |\n| **WHAT** | Negative patch evidence + live plugin + live user config + docs cross-check. |\n| **HOW CERTAIN** | **Evidence-based** (file:line-verified; patch absence is definitive). |\n| **WHAT-NOT-TESTED** | Did NOT probe v2 beta's `providers.*.settings` for a renamed `chunkTimeout` equivalent; did NOT test `opencode2 models` cache-merge path with the same plugin installed (v2 plugin API is breaking — `v2/docs/migrate-v1#plugins` says \"V1 plugins will not work in V2\"). |\n| **Errata on seed** | Seed \"models.dev catalog grok-patch, version suffix pp3g-fork\" as *fork* deltas is partially mislocated: grok patch is user-level plugin, version suffix is build-time define (D7), not a `models.dev` fetch patch. Corrected above. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Cross-cutting notes\n\n- **Wrapper drift guard (#274) is load-bearing.** `~/.local/bin/opencode` checks `grep -ac 'Body read timed out' >=2` *and* falls back to `--version` contains `fork`. This fails closed if the fork is replaced by stock — the desired behaviour for the silent-hang class. `~/.local/bin/opencode` also mangles `models.json` cache (hy3-preview synthesis, nvidia 9-model keep-list) before `exec`. Those are wrapper concerns, not fork binary concerns, and survive fork retirement if the wrapper file is kept.\n- **Fork DB channel** (`opencode-fork-pp3g.db`) is already in upstream `InstallationChannel` contract (`database.ts:49–54`): any channel value selects a separate DB. Only the `fork-pp3g` value is fork-only; the isolation *capability* is already upstream.\n- **Upstream now has adjacent fixes** but no parity for the core hang legs: v1.18.11 (MCP SSE reconnect loops), v1.18.14 (mid-stream structured errors → retries), v1.18.17 (generic retry cap + jitter), v1.18.20 (xAI capacity retries). None verbally matches D1/D2/D3 strings (`Body read timed out`, `Turn stalled`, `safeIterable`). The generic retry cap is the closest landing (maps to D4 partially).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Recommendation — Fork-necessity verdict (read-only R3 probe)\n\n### Verdict: **NO — retire-fork-now is NOT viable. Conditional retirement only, gated on D3 + D2 upstream parity with a functional gate.**\n\n| Option | Viability | Gate |\n|--------|-----------|------|\n| **Retire now, run stock 1.18.21** | **NOT VIABLE** | D3 (deadlock) + D2 (turn-level) are still absent from upstream v1 tip (verified via live fetch of dev `config.ts` + changelog verbatim search). Retiring re-introduces the indefinite-hang failure class the reliability epic (#156) closed — the historical killer for kickoff agents. |\n| **Retire on v1 with upstream patch** | **Conditional** | Land D3 + D2 (+ D1 for completeness) into upstream `dev`, verify via an *actual* hang-matrix run (the cheapest discriminating test per AGENTS.md) that `Body read timed out` / `Turn stalled` fire with `exit 1` not `124` and 3-POST budget, then retire. D4 partial landing helps but needs the per-code `RETRY_BOUNDED_CODES` semantics pinned. Wrapper guard should stay until the first post-retirement tagged release is confirmed to carry the strings. |\n| **Migrate to `opencode2` beta and retire** | **NO** | Beta is explicitly breaking (`opencode.ai/v2/docs/migrate-v1`: plugin API broken, server API revised, provider schema `provider`→`providers` + `options`→`settings/headers/body`). Fork deltas have not been probed against the beta's new `SessionExecution` / `providers` shapes, and v1 plugins (including the grok blacklist) do not run on beta. Treating beta as a fork replacement without that probe trades one class of hang for migration breakage. |\n| **Retire binary but keep wrapper + plugin** | **Already true and recommended** | The fork's safety-relevant *behaviour* is in the binary (D1–D3); the grok/timeout hygiene (D9) is in the wrapper + user-level plugin + `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json`, which survive binary swap independently. Do NOT delete them on fork retirement — they are orthogonal controls. |\n\n**Narrowest safe conditional:** D3 (`safeIterable` deadlock fix) landed + D2 (`llmIdleTimeout`/`timeoutOrElse`) landed + functional gate 16-row matrix (`fork/harness/run-matrix.sh` with `FORK_SRC` override or equivalent) passes (hang rows: marker present, no `124`; healthy rows: no false abort; row 16 guard counts correct). D1 is defence-in-depth companion, strongly recommended but the turn-level guard (D2) is the only bound above the body layer, so D2 is the gating item alongside D3.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Evidence pointers (file:line / URL)\n\n- Fork patch (958 lines): `git show 792cdbe3:fork/patches/opencode-fork-v1.18.13-pp3g.patch` → `diff --git` 9 files listed above; cached at `/tmp/opencode/r3/patch.diff`.\n- Live patched source: `fork/opencode-src/packages/opencode/src/provider/provider.ts:89,1826,1867` (wrapBodyIdle); `fork/opencode-src/packages/core/src/aisdk.ts:77,206`; `fork/opencode-src/packages/opencode/src/session/llm.ts:43–60` (safeIterable), `411–436` (llmIdleTimeout); `fork/opencode-src/packages/opencode/src/session/retry.ts:30,213`; `fork/opencode-src/packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts:235–238`; `fork/opencode-src/packages/core/src/installation/version.ts:6`; `fork/opencode-src/packages/core/src/database/database.ts:49–54`.\n- Wrapper: `~/.local/bin/opencode: FORK_MARKER='Body read timed out' / FORK_MARKER_MIN=2 / lineage comment #154/#138/#142/#129 / backup path ~/.local/share/opencode/fork-backups/20260808-233133/`.\n- Plugin + timeouts: `~/.config/opencode/plugins/plugin.ts:FORBIDDEN_MODEL_PATTERNS + opencode-go blacklist + FORBIDDEN sweep` ; `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json:provider.opencode/go.options.{timeout:3600000,headerTimeout:300000,chunkTimeout:300000}`.\n- Knowledge / docs: `.crosslink/knowledge/model-discipline.md` (Grok ban, chunkTimeout table); `docs/research/agent-tooling-and-permission-enforcement.md:§2.1,§2.7,§4` (fork DB, safeIterable, whitelist).\n- Upstream live fetch: `opencode.ai/changelog` (v1.18.11/14/17/20 entries quoted); `opencode.ai/docs/config#models` (chunkTimeout docs); `opencode.ai/v2/docs` + `v2/docs/migrate-v1` (provider schema split, accepted-but-unsupported fields, beta `opencode2` binary); `github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/dev/packages/core/src/v1/config/config.ts` raw (192 lines, experimental lacks llmIdleTimeout — fetched 2026-08-23).\n- Changelog cross-check: upstream dev `config.ts` fetched raw shows NO `llmIdleTimeout` / `bodyIdleTimeout` / `bodyAbsoluteTimeout`; `v2/docs/migrate-v1#accepted-but-unsupported-fields` does not list them (negative evidence of absence as new fields).\n\n---\n\n## 5. What-not-tested (explicit negative space, per AGENTS.md)\n\n1. Did NOT execute `fork/harness/run-matrix.sh` 16-row functional gate (nor the SDK unit tests) against stock `1.18.21`, the live fork binary, or `opencode2` beta — the cheapest discriminating probe for D1–D3. Verdict's conditional gate requires it.\n2. Did NOT probe `opencode2` beta's resolved provider/llm config schema or running binary for renamed equivalents (`providers.*.settings`, `experimental` new shape) — v2 parity for D1/D2/D4 remains `UNKNOWN-NEEDS-PROBE` beyond verbal docs.\n3. Did NOT fetch upstream `packages/opencode/src/session/llm.ts` or `provider.ts` HEAD to compare `safeIterable` / `RETRY_BOUNDED_CODES` textual absence line-for-line; used changelog verbal search + fork patch diff + dev `config.ts` as proxy for v1 tip.\n4. Did NOT re-run `opencode models opencode-go` catalog freshness against `opencode.ai/zen/go/v1/models` to confirm grok still ships in built-in catalog absent the plugin (relying on plugin's premise and changelog silence).\n5. Did NOT test wrapper drift-guard fallback path (`--version` contains `fork`) after a simulated fork rebuild that renames marker strings.\n\n---\n\n*Sources fetched 2026-08-23; fork pinned at `a105350` (stock) / patch at `792cdbe3` / live source identical to `9e898aa1` (+ #273 pin). Scratch at `/tmp/opencode/r3/patch.diff`. No repository writes in this pass.*","created_at":"2026-08-23T20:21:25.686837051Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:kpmhg3j+qTk/mZOq89IkcgZ64NhYgHNB1rXTy7a6WxI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg5uLAnDeBey6J8bcLYPT4aRDQh3oVDuXEUYhs4qgPfxAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAuweD+E5UczRd1AduyPfdNkG2moT2qgtHVNrbQlZMgXIY0doN9Th1zXBAktl3fU5+Vt/KQ2LYgFjQnhgeAfIFCg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:kpmhg3j+qTk/mZOq89IkcgZ64NhYgHNB1rXTy7a6WxI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg5uLAnDeBey6J8bcLYPT4aRDQh3oVDuXEUYhs4qgPfxAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHAI2Pr8zsKDQeWb8MkhqtL5vNQAWI+xnpGKNhpRDZXeGSmTItRZzwI5dqcdA0jGxOuq1ZJwj9MPqZRRpAwSvgc="}
